<title>GERMANY: West German Jan adjusted jobless rises 78,000.</title>
<headline>West German Jan adjusted jobless rises 78,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 Jan 97	  Dec 96	   Jan 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    3.266 million     2.961 million	2.901 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.029 million     2.951 million	2.686 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +78,000	  +23,000	   +21,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		10.6 pct	 9.6 pct	  9.4 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	224,457	 157,972	  212,521</p>
<p> Vacancies		   252,181	 221,967	  251,402</p>
<p>Change in number in work Nov 96 Oct 96</p>
<p>				 -40,000	 -30,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
